       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose is well above the labeled maximum for metformin.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1700 mg three times daily, which is **5100 mg/day**.\n- **Maximum:** The maximum is 2550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. Extended-release is capped at 2000 mg/day. A single dose is normally no more than 1000 mg.\n- **Risk:** This is twice the daily maximum. It raises the risk of severe GI effects and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the IR maximum)\n- **1700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals\n- **Another dose or frequency**\n\nIf you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
